  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **Storing a type the database hasn't stored before no longer deadlocks the connection pool.** The interner reads and mints type ids outside the unit of work's transaction, and took its connections from the pool units of work hold their transactions' connections from. A unit of work that held a taggregate's lock and stored a tevent of a new type, while units of work waiting for that lock held every connection of the pool, got no connection, and all of them waited until the pool timed out, 15 s by default: the SQL Server tevent store's deadlock. The interner now takes its connections from a pool of its own on the database, of at most two connections, which the server shows as `Compze type id interner`'s: a database may have two connections more than before.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Abstractions 0.5.0-alpha (was 0.4.0-alpha), Compze.Sql.MicrosoftSql 0.8.0-alpha (was 0.5.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
